Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='settings', at=datetime(2026, 9, 21, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The app may set a secret and may never read one back', body="⚠️ *The app may set a secret, and may never read one back* (2026-09-21, chain `settings`, `docs/SETTINGS-PLAN-2026-09-19.md`; a second host has a browser and a tailnet identity, no shell). Each rule is a mechanism:\n- A secret is stored only by a tapped Secret card, whose name is a `suzatary_core::settings::Settable`, minted against the closed list the INSTANCE FILE declares it needs (the model's token, a channel's secrets, the two GitHub tokens, one per purpose) — never `secretspec.toml`, which also declares the signing password and the box's keys, so those are refused by absence, not by a blocklist.\n- The tap needs a `Tap`, pinned to one caller by a tree-walking test; the capability that writes is in NO record, so a verb that set a secret would not compile.\n- secretspec sets only a name its file declares, and a deployment's code root is read-only, so the first secret a verb asks for declares the names its instance derives (reading an instance writes nothing) in a file of its own under the state directory that `extends` the code root's (`secrets::Declarations`, named by its text's digest so no stale writer drops a newer name; `State::declare` writes it before the names move; `suzatary secretspec` prints it, 2026-10-13).\n- The value goes to `secretspec set` on STDIN, never argv (`/proc` publishes argv), and is `Secret`-wrapped from the byte it is parsed, so no log, error, refusal or response carries it. The card's outcome names the KEY and the Settings row says whether it RESOLVES — the whole read surface; `doctor` says the same.\n- Unchanged: `secretspec set` from a terminal is the operator's path; the four release and mail-transport secrets are settable only from a terminal; `web/e2e/overview.test.ts` proves the value never comes back over the wire (asserting on the CDP network log, not only the DOM).", rationale='Decided 2026-09-21 (chain settings, docs/SETTINGS-PLAN-2026-09-19.md): a second host has a browser and a tailnet identity, and no shell. secrets::Declarations was added 2026-10-13.', supersedes=()))